    "old": "<img class=\"internal\" alt=\"One elongation cycle of translation on the mRNA 5 prime AUG GGU GAA AAG 3 prime. Panel 1: the ribosome covers codons GGU and GAA. The P site holds the tRNA with anticodon CCA carrying the growing chain Met-Gly; a tRNA with anticodon CUU carrying Glu enters the A site at codon GAA. Panel 2: a peptide bond forms and the chain Met-Gly is moved onto Glu, so the A-site tRNA now carries Met-Gly-Glu and the P-site tRNA is empty. Panel 3: translocation; the ribosome moves one codon toward the 3 prime end, the empty tRNA leaves, the tRNA carrying Met-Gly-Glu is now in the P site, and the A site is open at codon AAG for the next tRNA.\" width=\"760\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\" src=\"/@api/deki/files/512767/fig-p597179-elongation.svg\" fileid=\"512767\" />",
